        "original_id": "dd5b857b-e382-56c5-b162-f3135460614e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Krzysztof Penderecki\n- Works: Prelude for Clarinet in B-flat major, Prelude for Solo Clarinet, Threnody to the Victims of Hiroshima, Symphony No. 3, St. Luke Passion, Polish Requiem, Anaklasis, Utrenja\n- Topics: Penderecki compositions\n\nFacts:\n- Krzysztof Penderecki was a Polish composer.\n- Krzysztof Penderecki composed the Prelude for Clarinet in B-flat major, which is also referred to as Prelude for Solo Clarinet.\n- Krzysztof Penderecki's best known works include Threnody to the Victims of Hiroshima, Symphony No. 3, St. Luke Passion, Polish Requiem, Anaklasis, and Utrenja.\n- Krzysztof Penderecki composed four operas, eight symphonies, other orchestral pieces, a variety of instrumental concertos, choral settings mainly of religious texts, and chamber and instrumental works.",
